## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical E2E skills: gating UX with feature flags, deterministic tests, data seeding, and test isolation using Cypress or Playwright.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flags and gating
- Test data seeding per run
- LocalStorage state as idempotence marker
- Network/mocks to deterministically simulate flag responses
- Time-bounded execution for beginner scenarios

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright skeleton
test('onboarding respects flag', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/flags**', r => r.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ onboarding: true }) }));
  await page.goto('https://app.local/');
  await expect(page.locator('#onboard-modal')).toBeVisible();
  await page.locator('#finish').click();
  const stored = await page.evaluate(() => localStorage.getItem('onboarding_complete'));
  expect(stored).toBe('true');
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#onboard-modal')).toBeHidden();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this to multi-tenant setups with per-tenant flag overrides?
- How would you ensure the test remains reliable when the flag toggles during a session?

## Why This Is Asked

Feature-flag testing in multi-tenant, privacy-focused applications is common at scale. This question evaluates understanding of determinism, data isolation, and resilience under failure conditions.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant test isolation
- Feature-flag gating and consent API mocking
- Tenant-scoped headers and data boundaries
- Resilience: 503 handling with exponential backoff
- Desktop and mobile parity in UI and data latency

## Code Example

```javascript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('privacy flag rollout across tenants', async ({ page }) => {
  // Seed tenants A (flag on) and B (flag off)
  const tenantA = await seedTenant({ dataSharingEnabled: true });
  const tenantB = await seedTenant({ dataSharingEnabled: false });

  // Mock feature-flag and consent services
  await page.route('**/api/feature-flags', (route) => {
    const tenantId = route.request().headers()['x-tenant-id'];
    route.fulfill({
      status: 200,
      contentType: 'application/json',
      body: JSON.stringify({
        dataSharing: tenantId === tenantA.id
      })
    });
  });

  await page.route('**/api/consent', (route) => {
    route.fulfill({ status: 200, contentType: 'application/json', body: JSON.stringify({ granted: true }) });
  });

  // Verify tenant A sees dashboard
  await page.goto(`/dashboard`, { headers: { 'x-tenant-id': tenantA.id } });
  await expect(page.locator('[data-testid="dashboard-content"]')).toBeVisible();

  // Verify tenant B is blocked
  await page.goto(`/dashboard`, { headers: { 'x-tenant-id': tenantB.id } });
  await expect(page.locator('[data-testid="dashboard-content"]')).not.toBeVisible();

  // Validate tenant-scoped headers in API calls
  const apiRequest = page.waitForRequest('**/api/analytics/**');
  await page.goto(`/dashboard`, { headers: { 'x-tenant-id': tenantA.id } });
  expect((await apiRequest).headers()['x-tenant-id']).toBe(tenantA.id);

  // Test 503 retry with exponential backoff
  let attempts = 0;
  await page.route('**/api/analytics/**', (route) => {
    attempts++;
    if (attempts < 3) {
      route.fulfill({ status: 503 });
    } else {
      route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ latency: 120 }) });
    }
  });

  // Desktop and mobile parity
  for (const viewport of [{ width: 1280, height: 720 }, { width: 375, height: 667 }]) {
    await page.setViewportSize(viewport);
    await page.goto(`/dashboard`, { headers: { 'x-tenant-id': tenantA.id } });
    await expect(page.locator('[data-testid="dashboard-content"]')).toBeVisible();
    await expect(page.locator('[data-testid="dashboard-latency"]')).toHaveText(/\d+ms/);
  }
});
```

