## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design end-to-end checks for multi-tenant isolation, safe canary rollouts, per-tenant quotas, and rollback safety, all under realistic load patterns and with observability built in.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant data isolation and namespaces
- Canary feature flag rollout and traffic shaping
- Per-tenant quotas and burst load handling
- Data leakage prevention across tenants
- Rollback safety and path reversions
- Observability: traces, metrics, logs, alerting

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: toggle canary flag for a tenant and verify routing change
async function testCanaryTenant(tenantId){
  await api.setFeatureFlag({tenantId, flag: 'NEW_SEARCH', value: true, rollout: 0.2});
  const traces = await tracing.collect(tenantId);
  const path = traces.find(t => t.name === 'searchBackend');
  assert(path.usedNewBackend === true);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate rollback safety under observed latency spikes?
- What metrics and alerting thresholds would you define for this rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests offline-first, multi-region flows with eventual consistency and idempotency, a common real-world pain point in global apps.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end coverage across regions
- Deterministic mocks for external services
- Data isolation per tenant
- Idempotent submissions and reconciliation after outages
- CI-friendly parallelization

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Playwright test skeleton
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('offline-first order flow', async ({ page }) => {
  await login(page);
  await seedInventory(page, 'RegionA', {sku:'ABC', stock:5});
  await gotoCart(page);
  // Simulate offline
  await page.context().setOffline(true);
  await addToCart(page, 'ABC');
  await page.context().setOffline(false);
  await placeOrder(page);
  await expect(getPaymentStatus()).toBe('COMPLETED');
  // Additional checks omitted for brevity
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you structure mocks to ensure cross-region determinism across CI runs?
- What metrics and retries would you implement to detect and mitigate flakiness?

